+    The attributes EGL_YUV_COLOR_SPACE_HINT_EXT and EGL_SAMPLE_RANGE_HINT_EXT
+    may optionally be specified to select the YCbCr to RGB conversion.
+    EGL_YUV_COLOR_SPACE_HINT_EXT is one of EGL_ITU_REC601_EXT,
+    EGL_ITU_REC709_EXT, EGL_ITU_REC2020_EXT or EGL_SMPTE_240M_ANGLE, and
+    defaults to EGL_ITU_REC601_EXT. EGL_SAMPLE_RANGE_HINT_EXT is one of
+    EGL_YUV_NARROW_RANGE_EXT or EGL_YUV_FULL_RANGE_EXT, and defaults to
+    EGL_YUV_NARROW_RANGE_EXT. Other values generate EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE.
+    Specifying either attribute for other internal formats generates
+    EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE, as a non-zero EGL_IOSURFACE_ORIENTATION_ANGLE does.
+
+    The attribute EGL_IOSURFACE_ORIENTATION_ANGLE may optionally be specified
+    as a combination of the bits EGL_IOSURFACE_ORIENTATION_INVERT_X_ANGLE,
+    EGL_IOSURFACE_ORIENTATION_INVERT_Y_ANGLE and
+    EGL_IOSURFACE_ORIENTATION_SWAP_XY_ANGLE, and defaults to 0. Other bits
+    generate EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE. A non-zero value for other internal formats
+    generates EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE. The attribute describes how <buffer> maps to
+    the texture image of the pbuffer: the texel at normalized coordinates
+    (s, t) of the texture image is the RGB conversion of <buffer> sampled at
+    normalized coordinates computed by the following steps:
+      - If EGL_IOSURFACE_ORIENTATION_INVERT_Y_ANGLE is set, t becomes 1 - t.
+      - If EGL_IOSURFACE_ORIENTATION_INVERT_X_ANGLE is set, s becomes 1 - s.
+      - If EGL_IOSURFACE_ORIENTATION_SWAP_XY_ANGLE is set, (s, t) becomes
+        (t, s).
+
+    A texture bound to such a pbuffer can only be used as the source of
+    glCopyTextureCHROMIUM and glCopySubTextureCHROMIUM, which copy the texture
+    image defined above. Such a pbuffer cannot be made current: if <draw> or
+    <read> of eglMakeCurrent is such a pbuffer, EGL_BAD_MATCH is generated."
